{#- Grant eligibility body. The surrounding frame (render.py) always adds the required
    metadata, assumptions, missing information, sources and limitations sections, so this
    template lays out each program's match. Only the tags documented in render.py
    (headings, paragraphs, lists, tables, strong, em) survive conversion to Word. -#}
<h2>Summary</h2>
<p>
  {%- if not grants %}
  No reviewed grant programs could be checked against your answers yet. This is not a
  finding that no grant fits your project.
  {%- else %}
  We checked your answers against the published criteria of {{ grants | length }} grant
  program{{ "" if grants | length == 1 else "s" }}. Meeting every criterion we check does
  not mean an application will succeed: most programs are competitive and assess things we
  can't check, such as the quality of your plan.
  {%- endif %}
</p>

{% for g in grants %}
<h2>{{ g.title }}</h2>
<p>
  <strong>{{ g.status_label }}</strong> · Confidence: {{ g.confidence_label }} ·
  Applications: {{ g.intake_label }}
</p>
<p>{{ g.summary }}</p>
{% if g.funding %}<p><em>Funding: {{ g.funding }}</em></p>{% endif %}
<p>Run by {{ g.administrator }}. Details: {{ g.url }}</p>

<h3>Criteria we checked</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>Criterion</th><th>Your answers</th><th>What it means</th></tr>
  {% for c in g.criteria %}
  <tr>
    <td>{{ c.title }}</td>
    <td>{{ c.result_label }}</td>
    <td>{{ c.outcome or "" }}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{% if g.missing %}
<p>To finish this check, tell us: {{ g.missing | join("; ") }}.</p>
{% endif %}

<h3>Rounds</h3>
{% if g.rounds %}
<table>
  <tr><th>Round</th><th>Status today</th><th>Opens</th><th>Closes</th><th>Source</th></tr>
  {% for r in g.rounds %}
  <tr>
    <td>{{ r.title }}{% if r.note %}<br>{{ r.note }}{% endif %}</td>
    <td>{{ r.state_label }}</td>
    <td>{{ r.opens_on or "Not stated" }}</td>
    <td>{{ r.closes_on or "Not stated" }}</td>
    <td>{{ r.source }}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{% else %}
<p>We have no round dates we can cite for this program.</p>
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% if referrals %}
<h2>Who can help</h2>
<ul>
  {% for r in referrals %}<li>{{ r }}</li>{% endfor %}
</ul>
<p>These are kinds of professional, not recommendations of particular businesses.</p>
{% endif %}
